From e2ef0ab888f848ddea6b473b5b0b62aabc903886 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhangwenhao91 <zhangwenhao91@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:55:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [Ascend][Example] Paged MHA decode kernel over a fragmented
 KV cache

One block serves one (batch, head) pair and walks 128-row key tiles of a paged
KV cache with an online softmax; probabilities are packed in NZ layout. Pages
of 256 rows walk as two sub-blocks addressed through the page table at run
time, so a fragmented table costs nothing. The host side builds an additive
float32 attention bias (online softmax turns a fully cut tile into an exact
zero) and sanitizes NaN-poisoned unread pool rows. float16/bfloat16, causal
with no-key rows outputting zeros, seqlen_q <= 16, page_size 128*n.

On Ascend 950 a 256 MB cache sustains ~1.31 TB/s effective HBM bandwidth
(~91% of device copy bandwidth).
